\end{align*}
By adding the first and third equations, we can eliminate $\log y$ and get: \begin{align*}
\log x + \log z - \log y &= a - 7. \\
\end{align*}
Adding this to the second equation, we eliminate $\log z$ and get: \begin{align*}
\log x + \log z - \log y + \log y - \log z &= a - 7 + 15. \\
\log x &= a + 8. \\
\end{align*}
Substituting $\log x = a + 8$ into the first equation, we get: \begin{align*} a + 8 - \log y &= a, \\
\log y &= 8. \\
\end{align*}
Substituting $\log y = 8$ into the second equation, we get: \begin{align*} 8 - \log z &= 15, \\
\log z &= -7. \\
\end{align*}
Now, we can find $a$ by substituting $\log z = -7$ into the first equation: \begin{align*} a + 8 - 8 &= a, \\
a &= a. \\
\end{align*}
Hence, the value of $a$ is $\boxed{8}$. </think> <answer> 8 </answer>

